<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43497" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐβᾰφής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well steeped</i> or
				<i>dyed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.49.44
			</span></i> (dub. l.); <i>vivid</i>, of the colours of plants, Sabin.
			ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				9.17.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαφῶς</span> prob. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐαφῶς</span>
			 in Herod.
				Med.
			in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.72
			</span></i>:—so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐβαφία, ἡ</span>, 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐάφεια</span>
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				87
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐβαφῶν </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπόγγων</span>) 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐαφῶν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				4.21
			</span></i>.</div>
